  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The decay constant of a radioactive element is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.10\"></span> s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> the number of undecayed nuclei in a pure sample of this element is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5000\"></span>. How many nuclei are expected to decay in <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\"></span> s?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5000}{10e}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5000 - \\frac{5000}{10e}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5000}{e}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5000 - \\frac{5000}{e}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
